<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  SEA_FLOOR_AND_CATCH_PASS_1, 2026-09-24 — the Propane Lake's fishable
  shallow terrain, owed by design/Jawa/worldbuilding/sea_catch_rosters_
  2026-09-24.md's Propane Lake section.

  🔴 Why this def exists at all: the donor pair RUT_PropaneLake.xml points
  its RM_SeaShoreExtension at (AB_PropaneLake / AB_SolidPropane) is
  waterBodyType None (deep) / a non-water solid (shallow) — MEASURED
  against the decompiled engine 2026-09-23 (RimSage): WaterBodyTracker only
  forms a water body where waterBodyType != None
  (WaterBodyTracker.cs:50,:81,:178), Designator_ZoneAdd_Fishing refuses a
  None-type or Impassable cell (Designator_ZoneAdd_Fishing.cs:65), and
  FishingUtility returns nothing for a None body (FishingUtility.cs:138).
  So as shipped, no propane cell could ever hold a fishing zone no matter
  what the fishTypes table said. This terrain is the fix: a SHALLOW,
  PASSABLE, Saltwater-typed terrain laid as the shore's shallowTerrain so a
  fishing zone can actually form at the margin.

  ParentName="WaterShallowBase": the proven-safe parent this same pattern
  already uses for RUT_ScaldWaterOceanShallow (RUT_ScaldWater.xml) — Core's
  own Terrain_Water.xml carries a real Name="..." attribute on it, unlike
  Lake/Ocean/IceSheet's own BiomeDef tags.

  waterBodyType Saltwater, not Freshwater: DBH and every drink-from-terrain
  mechanism read Freshwater as potable, and RUT_PropaneLake.xml's own header
  states the donor terrain's None type was "correctly not recognised as
  drinkable water" — Saltwater keeps that non-potable property while still
  being a real water body the fishing system will recognise. tags Water is
  load-bearing for the same fishing-zone check.

  Look: reuses the donor AB_SolidPropane's own texture/render values so the
  new shallow reads as the same frozen-fuel crust the lake already shows —
  this is a mechanical fix, not new art (checked AB_SolidPropane's own
  fields via the live def dump before copying below).
-->
<Defs>

  <TerrainDef ParentName="WaterShallowBase">
    <defName>RUT_PropaneShallow</defName>
    <label>frozen propane shallows</label>
    <description>The margin of the lake, where the liquid fuel has frozen into a crust thin enough to break and drag a net through. Cold enough to burn an ungloved hand, and just barely open enough to be called water at all.</description>
    <renderPrecedence>396</renderPrecedence>
    <texturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/WaterShallowRamp</texturePath>
    <pollutedTexturePath>Terrain/Surfaces/WaterShallowRampPolluted</pollutedTexturePath>
    <waterDepthShader>Map/WaterDepth</waterDepthShader>
    <driesTo>AB_SolidPropane</driesTo>
    <canFreeze>false</canFreeze>
    <waterBodyType>Saltwater</waterBodyType>
    <avoidWander>true</avoidWander>
    <tags>
      <li>Water</li>
      <li>Ocean</li>
    </tags>
  </TerrainDef>

</Defs>
